# Measure Twice, Cut Once

## Measure Twice: Plan Before Drafting

Foggy work that will take more than one session: `/wayfinder` (see `AGENTS.md`).
A single-session design with no map: `/grill-with-docs`. Skip both for obvious
single-step changes. Ordinary one-slice features and bugs the user is sitting
with: Plan mode or implement under `vo-lum-workflow`. `/conductor` is for AFK /
overnight, a durable `loop.md`, spec overnight, or dispatching a clear map.

## Cut Once: Implementation Handoff

End every implementation plan with a short `Implementation Recommendation`:

- **Skills:** split into **attach before coding** (shapes implementation) and
  **run after only if requested** (opt-in retro/review). Say so explicitly if
  none fit.
- **Why:** one sentence tied to the task shape (docs, UI, debugging, refactor,
  migration, packaging, review).

If the plan names any attach-before-coding skills, the first implementation todo
is: `Load recommended implementation skills/rules and confirm scope`. Never put
opt-in retro skills in startup todos, and never run a retro automatically.
